{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778976720497,"sessionID":"ses_1ccbc19d4ffeMhaCiVvygDpbuM","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_dPHdHtYENEBTsi1oVQ6CgHbc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+`MONDO:0023243` has been obsoleted and given a direct replacement to `MONDO:0011274` (`Muenke syndrome`), based on the issue discussion and the cited review indicating the original Glass family was later recognized as Muenke syndrome.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Obsoleted `MONDO:0023243` (`glass-chapman-hockley syndrome`) with direct replacement by `MONDO:0011274` (`Muenke syndrome`).\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The imported issue requested deprecation of `glass-chapman-hockley syndrome`.\n+- The issue discussion cited `PMID:20108486`, and the reviewed article states that the original family reported by Glass was later found to harbor the FGFR3 P250R mutation of Muenke syndrome.\n+- `MONDO:0011274` already exists as the active MONDO term for Muenke syndrome, so this was handled as obsoletion with exact replacement rather than as a separate retained disease concept.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Renamed the term to `obsolete glass-chapman-hockley syndrome`.\n+- Replaced the old descriptive definition/comment block with an obsolete definition citing `PMID:20108486` and `GARD:0002479`.\n+- Removed logical axioms from the obsolete term.\n+- Marked mapped xrefs as `MONDO:obsoleteEquivalent`.\n+- Added `property_value: IAO:0000231 MONDO:TermsMerged`.\n+- Added `is_obsolete: true` and `replaced_by: MONDO:0011274`.\n+- Preserved the issue tracker link to `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9798`.\n+\n+Validation and review checklist:\n+- [x] Read imported issue title/body/comments from `__issue_context__.json`\n+- [x] Confirmed both `MONDO:0023243` and `MONDO:0011274` exist in 